-- title:
--   Quadratic Galois relation on Eisenstein torsion of J₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and suppose `HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar p` holds, i.e. the operators `heckeOperatorBar p ℓ` (the degree-preserving Hecke correspondences acting as $\mathbb{Z}$-endomorphisms of $J_0(p)$) commute pairwise for all primes $\ell,\ell'$; here $J_0(p) =$ `JZero p` is the group of degree-zero divisor classes modulo principal divisors of the modular function field of level $p$ base-changed to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, equipped with its action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}) = \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and, via `heckeModuleBar p`, with the module structure over `HeckeAlg` $= \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ in which $X_\ell$ acts by `heckeOperatorBar p ℓ`. Let $q$ be a prime, $\sigma$ a $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $\zeta \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and $a \in \mathbb{N}$ with $\sigma(\zeta) = \zeta^{a}$. Let $x \in J_0(p)$ be annihilated by the Eisenstein maximal ideal `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q`, the preimage under the $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra map `eisensteinEval p` (evaluation of the variables at the family `eisensteinSystem p`) of the ideal of $\mathbb{Z}$ generated by $q$; that is, $x$ lies in the torsion submodule cut out by that set of elements of `HeckeAlg`. Then $\sigma\cdot(\sigma\cdot x) - (1+a)(\sigma\cdot x) + a\,x = 0$.
--
--   This is the Galois-theoretic step behind Mazur's observation that the kernel of an Eisenstein prime is an admissible Galois module: the relation $(\sigma-1)(\sigma-\chi_q(\sigma))x = 0$ holds for every $\sigma$, the exponent $a$ recording the mod-$q$ cyclotomic character through $\sigma(\zeta)=\zeta^a$. It is used in the construction of the Mazur-admissible structure on the Eisenstein-primary torsion of $J_0(p)$, via [`ModularCurve.eisensteinPrimaryTorsion_isMazurAdmissible_heckeModuleBar`](thm.html#ModularCurve.eisensteinPrimaryTorsion_isMazurAdmissible_heckeModuleBar).
-- source:
